<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<knowl mode="exercise" xmlns="https://spatext.clontz.org" version="0.2">
    <content>
        <p>
<!-- {{#space}} -->
According to pi-Base, the space <url href="{{{url}}}">{{{name}}}</url> ({{uid}})
<!-- {{/space}} -->
must {{{target_must}}}. Explain how the human-proven properties and
theorems of pi-Base lead to this conclusion.
        </p>
    </content>
    <outtro>
        <p>
pi-Base deduces this using these given properties:
        </p>
        <list>
            <!-- {{#givens}} -->
            <item><p>{{{phrase}}}</p></item>
            <!-- {{/givens}} -->
        </list>
        <p>
and these
<url href="{{{proof_url}}}">{{theorem_count}} theorems</url>.
One valid argument:
        </p>
        <list>
            <!-- {{#steps}} -->
            <item><p>
By <url href="{{{theorem.url}}}">{{theorem.uid}}</url> ({{{theorem.statement}}}),
the space {{{conclusion}}}.
            </p></item>
            <!-- {{/steps}} -->
        </list>
    </outtro>
</knowl>
